{
  "id": "variable-time-schedule",
  "term": "variable-time schedule",
  "definition": "A variable-time schedule is a time-based, non-contingent schedule in which an event such as water delivery occurs at changing time intervals rather than at one constant interval. In learning research, it is used to study how varying the timing of deliveries affects behavior.",
